# Board patch paths, one per line in application order.
#
# The board keeps one storage route: KonaUfs publishes each root window as an IOMedia and
# IOStorageFamily answers the match (docs/porting/ufs.md: a root volume needs an IOKit media,
# not a BSD disk). The kebab bdevsw driver and its stubs are gone - kona-ufs-driver.patch,
# kona-hfs-noop.patch and kona-ufs-integration.patch - because a bdevsw disk publishes no
# IOMedia, APFS declines it before any block request, and its ufsroot0 device only added a
# second root candidate to IOFindBSDRoot.
#
# Root authentication: the 17.7.11 image is an unsealed owner root, so the check is reported
# and the boot continues until VerifiedRoot carries the policy.
kebab-route/kona-rootauth-bypass.patch
# konacp 5-8: bsd_init checkpoints around net_init_run/inittodr/vfs_mountroot.
kebab-route/kona-mountroot-cp.patch
# konacp 10: list the filesystems that carry a mountroot routine.
kebab-route/kona-vfs-cp.patch
# Stage trace for every mountroot attempt: "mr try <fs>" before the call and "mr <fs> ret=<err>"
# after it, so the boot page says which file system was tried and what it returned when a
# mountroot path stops asking for blocks.
kebab-route/kona-mountroot-trace.patch
# Every process exit lands on the boot page with its name and status: launchd execs with an
# accepted signature and PID 1 then exits with status 0, so the trace says which process it
# actually was and what it returned.
kebab-route/kona-init-exit-trace.patch
